A boot profile an installation can be moved or copied with, and a reader that can be tested.

gow-native.boot (patch 25) stored absolute paths, so the recorded disc, card, saves and capture folders stopped being
found when the installation moved. Version 2 records the installation root relative to the boot file's own folder, then
the guest ELF and every path inside the installation as '@'-relative to that root, so the launcher, the pipeline's
first-run defaults (tools/pipeline/modules/common.ps1 Format-BootProfile) and this reader agree without either side
knowing where the installation is. Paths outside the installation (a player's ISO, AppData) stay absolute, and V1 files
keep working unchanged, so an older profile is not invalidated.
Parsing, root anchoring and disc resolution live in the header-only runtime/boot_profile.h, away from the environment
export and standalone.log redirect that stay in main.cpp, so tools/test/boot-profile.cpp can run the same reader through
gow_boot_profile_tests (part of verify) with a V2 relative root, a V2 absolute root, legacy V1 and a missing disc. That
test found two defects in the first draft: a trailing newline counted as the guest-ELF line, so a truncated profile was
accepted, and an empty file was read before the header check.
Explicit guest ELF arguments still win, as in patch 25. A missing recorded disc keeps the existing error.
Validated: the whole chain plus this patch applies in order on the pinned runtime commit, and gow_boot_profile_tests
passes against the patched header (g++ -std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -Werror). The runtime itself was not built here; its
Windows build and a gameplay start remain to be run.
diff --git a/PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/boot_profile.h b/PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/boot_profile.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/boot_profile.h
@@ -0,0 +1,125 @@
+// Relative gow-native.boot profiles (gow-native-pc, patch zzz-326).
+//
+// The launcher and the pipeline write GOW_NATIVE_BOOT_V2: the installation root relative to the profile's own folder,
+// then the guest ELF, then the runtime settings. Paths inside the installation carry a leading '@', so a copied or
+// moved installation keeps working. GOW_NATIVE_BOOT_V1 (absolute paths, no root line) is still read.
+//
+// Header-only and free of environment and current-directory side effects: main.cpp owns the standalone.log redirect and
+// the environment export, and tools/test/boot-profile.cpp exercises this parsing without building the runtime.
+#pragma once
+
+#include <filesystem>
+#include <optional>
+#include <string>
+#include <string_view>
+#include <system_error>
+#include <vector>
+
+namespace ps2x::boot
+{
+    struct Setting
+    {
+        std::string key;
+        std::string value;
+    };
+
+    struct Profile
+    {
+        std::filesystem::path root; // as recorded; empty when the profile has no root line
+        std::string elf;            // as recorded: '@'-relative or absolute
+        std::vector<Setting> settings;
+        bool legacy = false; // V1: absolute paths, no installation root
+    };
+
+    inline constexpr char kMarker = '@';
+
+    inline bool IsRuntimeSetting(std::string_view key)
+    {
+        return key.starts_with("TOBIICHI_") || key.starts_with("PS2X_") || key.starts_with("GOW_");
+    }
+
+    // UTF-8 text (what the launcher and the pipeline write) as a path, including a player's non-ASCII folder. u8path is
+    // used by the older readers but is deprecated in C++20, so build the path from char8_t instead.
+    inline std::filesystem::path Utf8Path(std::string_view text)
+    {
+        return std::filesystem::path(std::u8string(reinterpret_cast<const char8_t *>(text.data()), text.size()));
+    }
+
+    // '@x' is inside the installation; anything else (an absolute path, a number, a switch) is taken as written.
+    inline bool IsRelativeValue(std::string_view value)
+    {
+        return !value.empty() && value.front() == kMarker;
+    }
+
+    // std::nullopt for an unknown header or a missing guest-ELF line; malformed setting lines are ignored, as before.
+    inline std::optional<Profile> Parse(std::string_view text)
+    {
+        // A final newline ends the last line; it must not count as an extra (empty) guest-ELF line.
+        std::vector<std::string_view> lines;
+        while (!text.empty())
+        {
+            const auto end = text.find('\n');
+            auto line = text.substr(0, end);
+            if (!line.empty() && line.back() == '\r') line.remove_suffix(1); // hand-edited or CRLF-checkout file
+            lines.push_back(line);
+            if (end == std::string_view::npos) break;
+            text.remove_prefix(end + 1);
+        }
+        if (lines.empty()) return std::nullopt;
+
+        Profile profile;
+        std::size_t next = 1;
+        if (lines[0] == "GOW_NATIVE_BOOT_V2")
+        {
+            if (next >= lines.size()) return std::nullopt;
+            profile.root = Utf8Path(lines[next++]);
+        }
+        else if (lines[0] == "GOW_NATIVE_BOOT_V1")
+        {
+            profile.legacy = true;
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            return std::nullopt;
+        }
+        if (next >= lines.size()) return std::nullopt;
+        profile.elf = std::string(lines[next++]);
+        for (; next < lines.size(); ++next)
+        {
+            const auto split = lines[next].find('=');
+            if (split == std::string_view::npos) continue;
+            auto key = std::string(lines[next].substr(0, split));
+            if (!IsRuntimeSetting(key)) continue;
+            profile.settings.push_back({std::move(key), std::string(lines[next].substr(split + 1))});
+        }
+        return profile;
+    }
+
+    // The installation root anchored to the profile's folder, so the file itself does not depend on where it lives.
+    inline std::filesystem::path RootPath(const Profile &profile, const std::filesystem::path &bootFolder)
+    {
+        if (profile.root.empty()) return bootFolder.lexically_normal();
+        if (profile.root.is_absolute()) return profile.root.lexically_normal();
+        return (bootFolder / profile.root).lexically_normal();
+    }
+
+    // Absolute location of a recorded path; '@x' resolves against RootPath.
+    inline std::filesystem::path ResolvePath(const Profile &profile, const std::filesystem::path &bootFolder,
+                                             std::string_view value)
+    {
+        const auto root = RootPath(profile, bootFolder);
+        auto path = IsRelativeValue(value) ? (root / Utf8Path(value.substr(1))).lexically_normal() : Utf8Path(value);
+        if (path.is_relative()) path = root / path;
+        if (!path.is_absolute()) path = std::filesystem::absolute(path);
+        return path.lexically_normal();
+    }
+
+    // The guest ELF, absolute; std::nullopt when the recorded disc is missing.
+    inline std::optional<std::filesystem::path> GuestElf(const Profile &profile, const std::filesystem::path &bootFolder)
+    {
+        const auto path = ResolvePath(profile, bootFolder, profile.elf);
+        std::error_code error;
+        if (!std::filesystem::is_regular_file(path, error)) return std::nullopt;
+        return path;
+    }
+}
